  "body": "## What and why\n\nAdd the two contributor procedures requested in #3913.\n\n- `takeover` requires author approval or the existing stale-claim evidence. It preserves claim, writer and reviewer ownership.\n- It explains maintainer-edit permissions, refresh timing, plain pushes and the patch-comment fallback after a refused push.\n- `repro-first` requires an actual MCP reading or failing pinning test before the implementation fix.\n- It stops when current main does not reproduce the bug. It records unsupported, prose-only and known-fail cases separately.\n- Add the two routing rows in `AGENTS.md` and an issue-specific decision record.\n\nThe text is original. No SolidCraft source was copied. No CAM code, workflow, dependency or `PROCESS_VERSION` changed.\n\n## Before and after\n\nBefore: `.claude/skills/takeover/` and `.claude/skills/repro-first/` were absent on fetched main `903e420b3a6443330233d3e58386d84100a21c5e`. The routing table had neither entry.\n\nAfter: both skills exist, and the table names each skill once. Runtime reproduction is not applicable to this prose-only change.\n\n## Actual checks\n\nChecks ran on final head `7f61f8feea9f4da2943a2985628c099e2a3cf08c`.\n\n- Focused text validator: 54 checks passed. It checks frontmatter, relative links, required steps, routing rows, policy references and the four-file diff scope.\n- `cargo test -p xtask ownership_contract_tests`: 13 passed. These existing tests cover the referenced ownership procedures, not execution of the new skills.\n- `cargo test -p xtask light_tests::the_law_names_the_light_lane_and_the_local_full_rerun -- --exact`: 1 passed. This existing test checks AGENTS.md law text.\n- `CAMCRAFT_GATE_JOBS=3 CAMCRAFT_GATE_SWEEP=off cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: executed; zero steps selected. This is not a test pass for the new documentation.\n- `git diff origin/main...HEAD --check`: passed.\n- `git merge-tree --write-tree origin/main HEAD`: clean against fetched main.\n\n## Limits\n\nNo existing focused suite directly tests these two new skills. The text checks do not prove agent execution or distributed exclusion.\n\nNo application, GUI, catalog, light, heavy or release build ran for this prose-only change. No physical machine was tested. `graphify` is unavailable in this environment; no graph update is reported.\n\nThis checkout uses canonical upstream as `origin`. Only the dedicated issue branch is published to the fork. The fork's main is not synchronized or changed.\n\nWriter record: https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/3913#issuecomment-7207223576\n\nEffort: medium\nChangelog: none\nProcess change: yes\n\nFixes #3913\n",
